  "behavior": [
    "Cache starts On beside the position bar. Exact checkpoints are collected approximately every five seconds and at requested destinations, within a 64-point / 8 MiB payload limit and LRU eviction.",
    "The 512-byte explicit little-endian versioned native state includes all voices, Wave RAM/index/counters, Noise seed/counters, DDA, LFO, selected/enabled channels, mute mask, clock/rate and output phase/history. No heap or native-object memcpy is used.",
    "App checkpoints also retain parser bank/stream graph and aliases, pending/fractional waits, queued PCM and ahead/committed Live timeline. Source identity, native settings and JS state are validated before restoring a fresh candidate.",
    "Stop and Code Run retain same-source points. Source/project replacement and channel-output changes invalidate them. A generation barrier prevents prefetched old-mix PCM being captured under a new mask.",
    "Off and Clear release points without moving playback, editing the instrument or cancelling paused audition. Unsupported or oversized checkpoints fall back to ordinary reconstruction.",
    "Cancel, superseding Seek, Stop, Code Run, source replacement and disposal cannot publish stale candidates. At most the retained reference core plus one candidate is active; cache entries own no native cores.",
    "Actual PCM tails and all semantic known/unknown Live settings match uncached Wave, LFO, Noise, direct DDA and looping DAC streams. Cross-history comparisons exclude only the revision UI counter, which counts observed same-frame transitions; same-history checkpoint continuation retains exact revision assertions.",
    "All eight suites use the same extracted standalone ZIP with readable browser/native rebuild sources. Desktop1240/mobile390 layouts were inspected."
  ],
